// §7's own worked example for the non-monotone fragment: intersection.
// `approve = editor & reviewer` (tools/schema-verifier/fixtures/schemas/
// non-monotone.authz) requires both relations to hold for the same
// subject at once — a real approval-workflow shape, not a contrived one.
// No constraints: this simply asks whether *any* user can ever be both
// editor and reviewer of the same document at the same time, which
// nothing in the schema forbids. Expected verdict: VIOLATED, up to
// k = 1 — the bounded search's own exhaustive enumeration tries the
// candidate subset {editor(o) = s, reviewer(o) = s} among others, and the
// real engine allows it.
invariant approve_reachable_via_intersection {
  s: user
  o: document

  goal: approve(s, o)
}
